photo":{"file":"photos/hottah.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 39: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam A). This image was acquired on Sep. 15, 2012 (Sol 39) at the local mean solar time of 13:30:24.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLA_400958632EDR_F0040468NCAM00422M_","sol":39}},{"id":"rocknest","sol":70,"name":"Rocknest","kind":"Sand samples","why":"Curiosity's first scoops, from a wind-blown sand drift. The first X-ray mineral analysis on Mars found volcanic minerals much like Hawaiian soil.","x":1346.5,"z":-1418.4,"lat":-4.59,"lon":137.44834,"elev":-4517.8,"photo":{"file":"photos/rocknest.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 70: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam A). This image was acquired on Oct. 17, 2012 (Sol 70) at the local mean solar time of 13:46:29.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLA_403711630EDR_F0050104NCAM00332M_","sol":70}},{"id":"johnklein","sol":182,"name":"John Klein (Yellowknife Bay)","kind":"First drilled rock","why":"The first hole ever drilled into a Mars rock. The grey mudstone holds clay minerals from a freshwater lake that could have supported microbes.","x":1393.1,"z":-1448.7,"lat":-4.58948,"lon":137.44913,"elev":-4520.5,"photo":{"file":"photos/johnklein.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 182: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam A). This image was acquired on Feb. 9, 2013 (Sol 182) at the local mean solar time of 11:53:04.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLA_413647373EDR_F0060000NCAM00225M_","sol":182}},{"id":"cumberland","sol":279,"name":"Cumberland (Yellowknife Bay)","kind":"Drilled rock","why":"Second drill hole in the lake mudstone. Its powder gave the first rock age measured on another planet and showed organic molecules.","x":1392.0,"z":-1449.0,"lat":-4.58948,"lon":137.44911,"elev":-4520.4,"photo":{"file":"photos/cumberland.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 279: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam B). This image was acquired on May. 19, 2013 (Sol 279) at the local mean solar time of 14:24:17.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLB_422267814EDR_F0060082NCAM00227M_","sol":279}},{"id":"shaler","sol":324,"name":"Shaler","kind":"Layered sandstone","why":"Tilted, criss-crossing sandstone layers laid down by a flowing stream. A ledge outcrop to study from the side.","x":1369.3,"z":-1406.1,"lat":-4.5902,"lon":137.44873,"elev":-4518.4,"photo":{"file":"photos/shaler.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 324: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam B). This image was acquired on Jul. 5, 2013 (Sol 324) at the local mean solar time of 14:55:17.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLB_426264574EDR_F0070000NCAM05133M_","sol":324}},{"id":"darwin","sol":395,"name":"Darwin (Waypoint 1)","kind":"Pebbly sandstone","why":"First science stop on the long drive toward Mount Sharp. Pebbly sandstone here records more ancient stream flow.","x":43.7,"z":-403.7,"lat":-4.60711,"lon":137.42629,"elev":-4505.7,"photo":{"file":"photos/darwin.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 396: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam B). This image was acquired on Sep. 17, 2013 (Sol 396) at the local mean solar time of 14:42:53.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLB_432655568EDR_F0160148NCAM00395M_","sol":396}},{"id":"cooperstown","sol":440,"name":"Cooperstown (Waypoint 2)","kind":"Rock outcrop","why":"A layered rock ledge examined with the arm instruments on the way to Mount Sharp.","x":-623.4,"z":498.5,"lat":-4.62233,"lon":137.415,"elev":-4493.7,"photo":{"file":"photos/cooperstown.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 440: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam B). This image was acquired on Nov. 1, 2013 (Sol 440) at the local mean solar time of 14:21:29.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLB_436560322EDR_F0220000NCAM00260M_","sol":440}},{"id":"dingogap","sol":535,"name":"Dingo Gap","kind":"Sand dune crossing","why":"Curiosity drove over a 1 m sand dune here to reach smoother ground, after sharp rocks had punctured its wheels. A lesson in choosing ground.","x":-1090.5,"z":750.7,"lat":-4.62659,"lon":137.40709,"elev":-4487.8,"photo":{"file":"photos/dingogap.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 535: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam B). This image was acquired on Feb. 6, 2014 (Sol 535) at the local mean solar time of 13:35:58.","credit":"NASA/JPL-Caltech","link":"https://mars.nasa.gov/msl/multimedia/raw-images/NLB_444991084EDR_F0260366NCAM00263M_","sol":535}},{"id":"windjana","sol":621,"name":"Windjana (The Kimberley)","kind":"Drilled sandstone","why":"Third drill hole, in sandstone where rock layers of different kinds meet. Rich in potassium minerals and manganese oxides.","x":-1390.9,"z":1477.0,"lat":-4.63884,"lon":137.40201,"elev":-4479.2,"photo":{"file":"photos/windjana.jpg","title":"Mars Curiosity Sol 621: Left Navigation Camera (Navcam)","caption":"NASA's Mars Curiosity rover acquired this image using its onboard Left Navigation Camera (Navcam B). Thi